\title{windsoropendata: Read City of Windsor Open Data in R}
\description{
A thin wrapper around \code{\link[arcgislayers:arc_read]{arcgislayers::arc_read()}} for the City of Windsor
open data portal (\url{https://open-data-portal-citywindsor.hub.arcgis.com/}).
The portal is an ArcGIS Hub site backed by the City's own ArcGIS Server
at \code{mappmycity.ca}, so the city is in the server name, not in the URL path.
}
\details{
Use \code{\link[=windsor_datasets]{windsor_datasets()}} to list what is available, \code{\link[=windsor_search]{windsor_search()}} to
find a dataset by name, and \code{\link[=windsor_get]{windsor_get()}} to read one by its short name,
for example \code{windsor_get("ward_boundaries")}. Live traffic speeds and
incidents come from the TomTom Traffic API instead, with
\code{\link[=windsor_tomtom_flow]{windsor_tomtom_flow()}} and \code{\link[=windsor_tomtom_incidents]{windsor_tomtom_incidents()}}, which need
a free TomTom API key in the \code{TOMTOM_API_KEY} environment variable.
}
